  "notes": "USAGE:\nFunctions as both a noun and a suru verb ({武装|ぶそう}する = to arm oneself). The past participle {武装|ぶそう}した is commonly used as a modifier meaning 'armed.' Frequently appears in news reporting about conflicts and security.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {武装|ぶそう}{解除|かいじょ}: disarmament\n- {武装|ぶそう}{勢力|せいりょく}: armed forces/groups\n- {武装|ぶそう}{集団|しゅうだん}: armed group\n- {完全|かんぜん}{武装|ぶそう}: fully armed\n- {武装|ぶそう}した{兵士|へいし}: armed soldier",
